            "review_text": "Lawrence M\nHigh Wycombe44 contributions\n0\nLooks inviting, and it is, but that's all.\nJan 2020\nII haven't visited Bui Vien since it was cleaned up, so out of interest, took a stroll down there. The Shamrock appeared attractive for three reasons:\n1. No \"Security\" staff outside attempting to usher you into a particular establishment (tip for business owners - this tactic turns most British customers off).\n2. It wasn't blasting non-stop techno \"music.\"\n3. There were no ladies used as enticement either.\n\nStaff? Very good.\nLive music? Spare me - I went twice (why)? On the first occasion, the male singer was massively off key several times as was the guitarist. On the second occasion, the lady lead singer was very good when you could hear her;she was constantly drowned ot by the musicians, and the keyboard player found it necessary to play that annoying \"stardust\" trill at every break or change of rhythm.\nPrices: Pretty high!\nFood can't say, but I wouldn't fancy trying it after standing next to the chef in the gents who went directly back into the kitchen still tucking himself away, no hand-washing at all, not even a rinse under the cold tap!\n\nFelt sorry for the young woman running as she seems very keen, but a little more attention to detail is needed.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 25, 2020",
